        "content": "<p>I have been working on principal fiber bundles and showing how an Ehresmann connection on such a bundle is equivalent to the affine connection on vector bundles. How, you might wonder, when Mathlib does not yet contain differential forms? I managed to fake enough of forms for my purposes, so for example I have:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">LieAlgebraValuedOneForm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">letI</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NormedAddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">TangentSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IG</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">show</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NormedAddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">EG</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inferInstance</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">letI</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NormedSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">TangentSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IG</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">show</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NormedSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">EG</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inferInstance</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">Cₛ</span><span class=\"bp\">^∞⟮</span><span class=\"n\">IB.prod</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IG</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">EB</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">EG</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">GroupLieAlgebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IG</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">_p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TotalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">EB</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">EG</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">GroupLieAlgebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IG</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"bp\">⟯</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>The principal example (pun absolutely intended) is the frame bundle — the fibers are ordered bases of the tangent bundle, isomorphic to GL(E), the general linear group.</p>\n<p>Naively I thought that in Mathlib I should take a fiber bundle and add more structure to it:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsPrincipalBundle</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">TopologicalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">ChartedSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">HG</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Group</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">LieGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IG</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∞</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TopologicalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">TopologicalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">TotalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">MulAction</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">MulOpposite</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">TotalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">ChartedSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ModelProd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">HB</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">HG</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">TotalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">IsManifold</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">IB.prod</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IG</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∞</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">TotalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">SmoothRightGAction</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∞</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IG</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">IB.prod</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IG</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">TotalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">FiberBundle</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">is_free</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TotalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">),</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">MulAction.stabilizer</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">MulOpposite</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊥</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">respects_fibres</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TotalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">proj</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p.proj</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">equivariant_triv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TotalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">),</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">trivializationAt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p.proj</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"o\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">p.proj</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">trivializationAt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p.proj</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"o\">⟩</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">smooth_proj</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ContMDiff</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">IB.prod</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IG</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IB</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∞</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TotalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p.proj</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>But Mathlib does not have a theory of smooth fiber bundles. Fortunately I was able to use the fact that GL(E) is an open subset of the vector bundle Hom(E, TM) and use the theory of vector bundles to prove e.g. that GL(E) is a smooth manifold.</p>\n<p>But now I am kind of stuck: GL(E) is not a <code>TotalSpace (E →L[𝕜] E)ˣ ...</code>. I was able to prove that GL(E) was homeomorphic to such a space, but then I ran into another problem: how do I transfer the manifold instance from GL(E) to this <code>TotalSpace</code>?</p>\n<p>And then I re-read Bleecker and discovered that his bundle is completely general, and in fact re-reading Schuller: <em>very roughly speaking, a principal fibre bundle is a bundle whose typical fibre is a Lie group</em>. In fact the fibers are torsors, and I believe  <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"646363\">@Ben Eltschig</span> is working on such a definition. I thought I would experiment and not actually use torsors (which to me at any rate don't seem to add much), so now I am in the middle of a refactoring.</p>\n<p>The reason I am posting this is to point out that any definition of a principal bundle must be able to support the example of the frame bundle, and also to once again feel sad about what is missing for differential geometry.</p>\n<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"634338\">@Michael Rothgang</span>  is it worth creating some sort of framework document with what is missing, who is working on what, and what PRs exist? I think there is some such concept in the Mathlib community — is this a \"blueprint\"?</p>\n<p>PS: I just wanted to mention the lack of quotient manifolds, which I think someone is working on.</p>",
        "id": 601091682,
        "sender_full_name": "Dominic Steinitz",
        "timestamp": 1780908275
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Just a short answer for now:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>quotient manifolds are being worked on (and in fact, virtually sorry-free). <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"934474\">@Pepa Montero Jimena</span> is cleaning up the code now and will PR it afterwards</li>\n<li><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"646363\">@Ben Eltschig</span> is working on principal bundles (though not necessarily the smooth case), and has thought more about this than I have this morning :-)</li>\n<li>indeed, we're missing a theory of smooth fiber bundles (and differential forms). Both are on my radar, but one step at a time :-)</li>\n<li>a blueprint is usually used to coordinate working on a distributed formalisation project (not to coordinate work between people, and not to track \"the overall state of an area\"). At the moment, I don't think there's much overlap or acute need to coordinate efforts. That said, I'm happy to post a progress update soon - what's being worked on, who's doing that, where help is useful, etc. Right now, that information lives in my head, but sharing it more widely is indeed a good idea.</li>\n</ul>",
        "id": 601096808,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Rothgang",
        "timestamp": 1780909775
    }
]